# Derived gemma4 with a context large enough for this agent.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: Ollama defaults num_ctx to 4096 regardless of what the
# model supports, and its OpenAI-compatible endpoint (/v1) silently ignores
# per-request `options`, so the agent CANNOT raise the context from code.
# At 4096 a normal turn here (~4.1k tokens of system prompt + tool schemas +
# history) overflows and Ollama drops the OLDEST tokens — which is the system
# prompt. The model then answers with no persona, no connector list and no
# grounding. Verified: with a codeword planted in the system prompt and a 6k
# filler turn, the default build could not repeat it; this build can.
#
# num_ctx is set to gemma4's full 262144. Measured on an M4/24GB: resident
# size stays ~8.3GB and 100% GPU, and prefill/generation speed is UNCHANGED
# versus 4096 (133 tok/s prefill, 12 tok/s generation either way) — the KV
# cache grows with tokens actually used, not with the declared ceiling, and
# Gemma's sliding-window attention keeps only a few global layers at full
# length. So the ceiling is effectively free; real cost is per-token prefill.
#
# Build:  ollama create gemma4:12b-majordomo -f deploy/ollama/Modelfile.gemma4-majordomo
# Use:    OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma4:12b-majordomo in the instance .env
#
# The alternative is OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=262144 on the server, but that is
# global to every model and needs `ollama serve` restarted; this is scoped.

FROM gemma4:12b

PARAMETER num_ctx 262144
